WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:05.650
Which Batman do people keep referencing in
"Peacemaker" and how could it tie into the

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:07.390
upcoming Flash movie?

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:12.379
Are these just jokes or are they actually
hidden secrets that only the cleverest fans

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:14.429
could find?

00:00:14.429 --> 00:00:19.520
Christopher Smith is living proof that a sucker
is born every minute on the internet.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.590
Throughout the first season of "Peacemaker,"
he reveals that Aquaman is mer-curious and

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:29.660
Superman loves to leap the tallest buildings
for a chance to snack on fresh butt burritos.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:34.340
Of course, these are only a handful of fun
facts about the Justice League that he's scoured

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:38.630
the internet for, and he treats every dubious
comments section as gospel.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.990
"You actually believe that shit?

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:45.870
He has an insane story for every single superhero."

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:49.900
The question is, how far do his conspiracy
theories reach?

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:54.559
It doesn't help that he came from a home where
his father was a racist and misogynist criminal

00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:59.390
who bought into every crackpot that monetizes
the spread of misinformation and division.

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:04.940
While the rest of Project Butterfly has poked
holes in his supposed facts about the world,

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:08.850
Peacemaker still holds onto an outrageous
belief system that would make the average

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.040
person question their sanity.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:16.330
The other somewhat unlikely possibility is
that these are, in fact, real facts in the

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:17.870
world of Peacemaker.

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:22.650
"I'm so f**king sick of that rumor."

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:24.090
"It's not a rumor."

00:01:26.697 --> 00:01:31.717
While it's common to include Easter eggs and
comic book references in superhero shows,

00:01:31.717 --> 00:01:36.497
John Economos' declaration to Peacemaker has
an interesting implication:

00:01:36.497 --> 00:01:39.997
"I'd rather be with f–king Bat-Mite than
you."

00:01:39.997 --> 00:01:40.997
"Who's Bat-Mite?"

00:01:40.997 --> 00:01:44.437
"He's a two foot tall interdimensional imp
who stans Batman.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.207
I'd rather be with him."

00:01:46.207 --> 00:01:49.617
It all but confirms the existence of Bat-Mite
in the DCEU.

00:01:49.617 --> 00:01:55.146
Fans have seen this pesky character appear
in other TV shows such as "The New Adventures

00:01:55.146 --> 00:01:59.907
of Batman" and "Batman: The Brave and the
Bold," but this is the first time he's been

00:01:59.907 --> 00:02:02.247
mentioned in a live-action show.

00:02:02.247 --> 00:02:07.596
On his official Instagram account, James Gunn
confirmed that Bat-Mite is now canon, but

00:02:07.596 --> 00:02:08.596
is he really?

00:02:08.596 --> 00:02:13.627
If he's not actually seen, how can anyone
actually be sure he exists?

00:02:13.627 --> 00:02:18.157
We'd better stop here before the philosophical
implications get overwhelming.

00:02:18.157 --> 00:02:23.497
It was a brave decision to turn Auggie Smith
into the White Dragon of the DCEU.

00:02:23.497 --> 00:02:28.517
In the context of the story and our understanding
of Peacemaker's troubled past, it was a natural

00:02:28.517 --> 00:02:33.227
fit to turn Auggie into the white supremacist
supervillain who led his son astray with a

00:02:33.227 --> 00:02:34.937
highly questionable upbringing.

00:02:34.937 --> 00:02:39.367
That said, there have been multiple versions
of the White Dragon in the comics.

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:44.417
So even though Auggie might be dead in "Peacemaker,"
he has a legion of followers who are more

00:02:44.417 --> 00:02:47.987
than likely to take up the mantle in the future.

00:02:47.987 --> 00:02:52.926
Ask Peacemaker who his best friend is and
there's only one answer: Eagly.

00:02:52.926 --> 00:02:57.187
To be fair, who wouldn't want to be BFFs with
an eagle that's capable of gouging out the

00:02:57.187 --> 00:03:00.267
eyes of enemies with both its beak and talons?

00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:06.117
Be that as it may, Vigilante might have something
to say about this current friendship hierarchy:

00:03:06.117 --> 00:03:07.117
Vigilante.

00:03:07.117 --> 00:03:11.637
"Just like an all-time classic run with my
best friend Peacemaker, my second best-friend

00:03:11.637 --> 00:03:14.417
Eagly, my fifth best friend Adebayo."

00:03:14.417 --> 00:03:19.116
There's no doubt in anyone's mind that Vigilante
looks up to Peacemaker and sees him as his

00:03:19.116 --> 00:03:20.597
only friend.

00:03:20.597 --> 00:03:25.216
Even though Peacemaker won't freely admit
it in the public, he does view Adrian Chase

00:03:25.216 --> 00:03:28.556
as a friend — albeit a bit of an annoying
one.

00:03:28.556 --> 00:03:32.116
That said, Vigilante has been there for him
when he's needed him the most.

00:03:32.116 --> 00:03:38.257
He might not be the most conventional of friends,
or a rational human being, but he hasn't let

00:03:38.257 --> 00:03:39.966
down Peacemaker yet.

00:03:39.966 --> 00:03:45.917
Maybe, just maybe, Vigilante may finally be
acknowledged as Peacemaker's best friend one

00:03:45.917 --> 00:03:46.917
day.

00:03:46.917 --> 00:03:48.907
Well, probably not.

00:03:48.907 --> 00:03:58.687
"Don't tell V, but after Eagly, you're my
BFF."

00:03:58.687 --> 00:04:03.597
Where exactly does "Peacemaker" fit in the
DC film universe's timeline?

00:04:03.597 --> 00:04:08.937
Judging by the events and characters, it takes
place immediately after "The Suicide Squad,"

00:04:08.937 --> 00:04:11.597
which is considered a part of the DCEU.

00:04:11.597 --> 00:04:15.576
In this timeline, the Batman is still Ben
Affleck's version of the Caped Crusader.

00:04:15.576 --> 00:04:19.946
However, this doesn't quite align with something
that Auggie's neighbor says to Peacemaker

00:04:19.946 --> 00:04:22.097
about the Dark Knight not killing.

00:04:22.097 --> 00:04:23.956
"Batman doesn't kill people."

00:04:23.956 --> 00:04:24.956
Because he's a pussy!"

00:04:24.956 --> 00:04:26.306
"He's a dark creature of the knight!"

00:04:26.306 --> 00:04:28.356
"He's a jackass!"

00:04:28.356 --> 00:04:33.496
Recalling the events of "Batman v Superman:
Dawn of Justice," Batman didn't straight-up

00:04:33.496 --> 00:04:38.437
murder criminals, but he didn't exactly pump
the brakes on the Batmobile to avoid crashing

00:04:38.437 --> 00:04:44.486
into them, nor did he exercise much restraint
in the brutal beatdowns he dished out, either.

00:04:44.486 --> 00:04:48.366
It sure looks like he kills at least a couple
of bad guys.

00:04:48.366 --> 00:04:53.216
One possibility here is that "Peacemaker"
might actually take place after the "Flash”

00:04:53.216 --> 00:04:54.216
movie.

00:04:54.216 --> 00:04:57.856
The upcoming movie will feature Barry Allen
breaking the timeline and crossing the streams

00:04:57.856 --> 00:05:02.567
of the multiverse, so in the process, he could
have brought in a new Batman who has much

00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:04.616
cleaner hands than Batfleck.

00:05:04.616 --> 00:05:09.407
Alternatively, we're reading too much into
what's most likely just a joke.

00:05:09.407 --> 00:05:13.136
Make no mistake about it, Christopher Smith
is a love machine.

00:05:13.136 --> 00:05:17.206
He's got all his love to give and all his
life to live.

00:05:17.206 --> 00:05:21.567
However, there's a revealing moment in the
episode "Murn After Reading" that indicates

00:05:21.567 --> 00:05:25.576
a midnight rendezvous that didn't quite finish
as expected.

00:05:25.576 --> 00:05:30.537
As a favor to Jamil, the janitor from the
hospital where Smith was, Peacemaker speaks

00:05:30.537 --> 00:05:34.466
to the local school in an effort to make Jamil's
child seem more popular.

00:05:34.466 --> 00:05:39.466
Naturally, the children ask him a lot of questions,
though there's one specific query that sticks

00:05:39.466 --> 00:05:44.787
out more than the others: A little girl holds
up her hand and asks Peacemaker if he remembers

00:05:44.787 --> 00:05:46.127
her mom Becky Coolidge.

00:05:46.127 --> 00:05:49.487
"I haven't seen her in like 10 years."

00:05:49.487 --> 00:05:52.847
"I think you might be my real dad."

00:05:52.847 --> 00:05:53.847
"What?"

00:05:53.847 --> 00:05:58.106
It's played like a joke, but it could be an
interesting plot thread for a future storyline.

00:05:58.106 --> 00:06:01.157
What if the little girl really is Peacemaker's
daughter?

00:06:01.157 --> 00:06:06.077
And what if her mother is someone who could
be linked to another superhero or villain?

00:06:06.077 --> 00:06:10.986
In the episode "Stop Dragon My Heart Around,"
it's implied that Peacemaker's sexuality is

00:06:10.986 --> 00:06:14.676
a bit more fluid than his general demeanor
might have implied.

00:06:14.676 --> 00:06:19.256
Series creator James Gunn himself revealed
to Empire Magazine that John Cena played a

00:06:19.256 --> 00:06:22.597
pivotal role in shaping the character's sexuality.

00:06:22.597 --> 00:06:23.616
Gunn said,

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:28.996
"John does improv all the time and he just
turned Christopher Smith into this hyper-sexualized

00:06:28.996 --> 00:06:32.106
dude that is open to anything sexually."

00:06:32.106 --> 00:06:37.067
Considering Peacemaker's openness to romantic
partners, there's a chance that he and Vigilante

00:06:37.067 --> 00:06:40.377
could develop into something more in the future
as well.

00:06:40.377 --> 00:06:45.136
The two of them share an intimate encounter
with Amber, so it isn't like they haven't

00:06:45.136 --> 00:06:47.566
had a close encounter of the bedroom kind.

00:06:47.566 --> 00:06:52.756
At the same time, it could go a long way to
explaining Vigilante's borderline obsession

00:06:52.756 --> 00:06:53.886
with Smith.

00:06:53.886 --> 00:06:58.236
What started off as a bond over violent crime
fighting could blossom into something more

00:06:58.236 --> 00:07:00.507
special and intimate between them.

00:07:00.507 --> 00:07:05.076
That said, the answer to this question is
"probably not" since "Peacemaker" ends with

00:07:05.076 --> 00:07:08.787
an implied bond between Chris and Harcourt.

00:07:08.787 --> 00:07:14.466
"Peacemaker ... What a joke."

00:07:14.466 --> 00:07:19.546
Rick Flag's line from "The Suicide Squad"
has haunted Smith ever since he killed Task

00:07:19.546 --> 00:07:21.416
Force X's leader.

00:07:21.416 --> 00:07:25.476
While he might have thought he had a very
good reason for doing so at the time, it still

00:07:25.476 --> 00:07:27.786
doesn't help ease his conscience.

00:07:27.786 --> 00:07:32.586
Ultimately, he was simply following orders,
which is something that Amanda Waller values

00:07:32.586 --> 00:07:34.246
more than anything else.

00:07:34.246 --> 00:07:37.606
She wants foot soldiers, not free thinkers,
on her team.

00:07:37.606 --> 00:07:41.567
So, could he find himself back on her team
in the future?

00:07:41.567 --> 00:07:45.947
After all, Peacemaker killing someone is nothing
new to the Suicide Squad.

00:07:45.947 --> 00:07:48.606
This is a team full of murderous superviallins.

00:07:48.606 --> 00:07:54.026
Peacemaker is no saint, but neither are any
of the criminals involved in Task Force X.

00:07:54.026 --> 00:07:58.307
Waller might still see a purpose for him,
so it's possible that she might call him up

00:07:58.307 --> 00:08:01.216
to the main team once again somewhere down
the line.

00:08:01.216 --> 00:08:06.897
"It's Cow or Never," the Season 1 finale of
"Peacemaker," features unexpected and epic

00:08:06.897 --> 00:08:09.087
cameos from the Justice League.

00:08:09.087 --> 00:08:13.976
While Wonder Woman and Superman are out of
focus and shown through the use of silhouettes,

00:08:13.976 --> 00:08:19.836
Jason Momoa's Aquaman and Ezra Miller's Flash
actually have lines and show their faces.

00:08:19.836 --> 00:08:24.536
However, there's one crucial member missing
from the lineup here: Batman.

00:08:24.536 --> 00:08:29.166
The Dark Knight's existence was already confirmed
in the series, so where's he hiding during

00:08:29.166 --> 00:08:30.166
this scene?

00:08:30.166 --> 00:08:32.327
Did the Batmobile break down or something?

00:08:32.327 --> 00:08:37.466
Again, this could give credence to the theory
that "Peacemaker" takes place after the "Flash"

00:08:37.466 --> 00:08:38.466
film.

00:08:38.466 --> 00:08:43.087
Considering the movie is set to be Batfleck's
swan song in the DCEU, there's a good chance

00:08:43.087 --> 00:08:46.987
that the Justice League might be a member
short for a while.

00:08:46.987 --> 00:08:51.957
No one expected Adebayo to go in front of
the world and confirm the existence of Task

00:08:51.957 --> 00:08:54.047
Force X and what it does.

00:08:54.047 --> 00:08:59.827
Perhaps even more shockingly, she exposes
her mother's identity and role in this program.

00:08:59.827 --> 00:09:04.356
It's an event that's likely to have major
repercussions and could result in Waller being

00:09:04.356 --> 00:09:07.476
removed as the puppet master of the Suicide
Squad.

00:09:07.476 --> 00:09:13.547
Yet despite Adebayo's revelations, there's
no chance that Task Force X will be shut down;

00:09:13.547 --> 00:09:16.096
it'll simply pop up under another guise.

00:09:16.096 --> 00:09:20.957
This might present an opportunity for someone
new to take the reins of Task Force X and

00:09:20.957 --> 00:09:22.327
the Suicide Squad.

00:09:22.327 --> 00:09:28.677
Adebayo is an improbable candidate since she
exposed the whole operation, but Emilia Harcourt

00:09:28.677 --> 00:09:30.726
could be in line for a major promotion.

00:09:30.726 --> 00:09:35.797
Her near-fatal injuries in the season finale
may move her out of the field and into an

00:09:35.797 --> 00:09:37.057
internal role.

00:09:37.057 --> 00:09:43.547
Perhaps a season 2 of "Peacemaker" could address
who takes over the vacancy at Task Force X.

